-- run: a derived function takes one evidence parameter per
-- entry of its inferred CONTEXT (the owner's decision, checker-v2.md §11.2).
-- `Holder`'s own `eq` needs `a.key`, so `Main`'s `Outer a`, which holds a
-- `Holder a`, derives `eq` with context `a.key` — not "`a.eq`, one per type
-- parameter" — and both comparisons call `Holder.eq`, which compares keys
-- only. Expected `True`, `True`.
--
-- Oracle twin: this project with `Outer` made monomorphic,
-- `type Outer = Outer (Holder.Holder Keyed.Keyed)`, prints `True`, `True`.
-- A derived ABI that asked `a.eq` of the parameter would refuse the second
-- comparison with NOT EQUATABLE `Outer Keyed`, since `Keyed`
-- has none.
pub type Holder a
    = Holder a


pub eq : Holder a, Holder a -> Bool
    where a.key : a, () -> Int
eq left right =
    case left of
        Holder l ->
            case right of
                Holder r ->
                    l.key () == r.key ()
